  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v1.1.0\n\n✨ New Features\n* GD-502: GdUnit0202: Test case names must be unique, reports TestCase attributes of a test method that set the same TestName,\n          contributed by @Tayrtahn.\n\n✨ Improvements\n* GD-478: The DataPoint attribute analysis caches the resolved types per compilation and runs faster, contributed by @Tayrtahn.\n* GD-520: The analyzers run with the .NET SDK 8.0.100 and Visual Studio 17.8 or newer, v1.0.0 needed the .NET SDK 9.0.300.\n          The package no longer adds the analyzers as a library reference to the projects that use it.\n\n🪲 Bug Fixes\n* GD-462: Fixing a stack overflow that crashes the compiler when a test or test hook calls a recursive method,\n          the Godot runtime check now stops on methods it is already analyzing.\n\nv1.0.0\nThis is the Initial release of the analyzers.\n\nGdUnit0201: Multiple TestCase attributes not allowed with DataPoint\nGdUnit0500: Godot Runtime Required for Test Class\nGdUnit0501: Godot Runtime Required for Test Method\n\nFeatures:\n- Compile-time validation of GdUnit4 attribute combinations\n- Provides clear error messages with method name identification\n- Integrates seamlessly with Visual Studio and other IDEs\n\nIntegration:\n- Built for .NET Standard 2.0 compatibility\n\nTechnical Details:\n- Implementation based on Roslyn analyzer framework\n- IDE support for real-time error detection\n- Includes a help link to documentation",
